ACG to Acquire Keşkek Licence to Extend Gold Production
LONDON, Sept. 7, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- ACG Metals Limited (""ACG"" or the ""Company"") is pleased to announce it has entered into a binding agreement with Meta Nikel Kobalt Madencilik Sanayi ve Ticaret A.Ş. (""META"") to acquire 100% of mining licence 60926 and all rights associated with it (together, the ""Licence""), which contains the Keşkek gold project (""Keşkek"" or the ""Project""), for an initial cash consideration of US$4 million plus potential contingent payments as described below.
Keşkek provides a new source of oxide ore within 70 km of ACG's Gediktepe mine in Türkiye and is expected to extend the utilisation of the Company's heap leach facility (the ""Facility"") by several years.
Highlights
Acquisition of the Licence, covering 666 hectares, for an initial cash consideration of US$4 million and potential deferred cash consideration of US$3.85 million at start of production in mid-2027.
