Cabbacis Files “X95” Worldwide Trademark Applications for Very-Low-Nicotine Cigarette Brand
NIAGARA FALLS, N.Y.--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Cabbacis (OTCQB: CABI), a U.S. federally-licensed tobacco-product manufacturer focused on risk-reduction products being developed under the iBLEND™ and X95™ brand names, today announced that it has filed worldwide trademark applications for its X95™ cigarette brand.
X95 is a patent-pending, very-low-nicotine, tobacco cigarette without any hemp and contains approximately 95 percent less nicotine than commercial cigarette brands.
Cabbacis has filed trademark applications for X95™ in the United States and numerous international markets: Europe, the United Kingdom, China, Japan, India, Indonesia, the Philippines, South Korea, Australia, New Zealand, Canada, Mexico, Chile and Brazil.
Cabbacis has also purchased and secured various “X95” domain names for the brand’s forthcoming website, including X95.world and X95cigs.com.
