Super Copper Commences Phase 2 Geophysics at the Castilla Project
VANCOUVER, BC, Sept. 8, 2026 /CNW/ -- SUPER COPPER CORP. (CSE: CUPR) (OTCQB: CUPPF) (FSE: N60) (""Super Copper"" or the ""Company""), is pleased to announce that it has commenced its Phase 2 Geophysics Program, which includes induced polarization (""IP"") and resistivity surveys at its 100%-owned Castilla Project (the ""Project""), located approximately 90 km south of Copiapo, Chile.
The IP program follows the Company's recently completed drone magnetic and hyperspectral surveys at Castilla, which outlined multiple kilometre-scale alteration patterns, magnetic bodies and identified a series of quartz-magnetite-copper vein systems at surface (see news release dated July 30, 2026). The next step is IP: it directly responds to the sulphide content of the veins and their potential source and is intended to help define drill targets at the Project.
