Domestic Metals Commences Drill Program at Smart Creek Project, Montana
VANCOUVER, British Columbia, Sept. 08, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Domestic Metals Corp. (the “Company” or “Domestic”) - (TSXV: DMCU; OTCQB: DMCUF; FSE: 03E0) is pleased to announce the commencement of the planned 9,000m diamond drill program at its Smart Creek Project in Montana (video and photos here). The program is designed to test high-grade porphyry copper style mineralization identified through the Company's 2025–2026 exploration campaign.
The Smart Creek Copper Porphyry Project, acquired in August 2024, is a joint venture with Rio Tinto, where Rio owns 40% of the asset. The project covers 8,000 hectares and is located 50km northwest of the Butte Mine Complex (the Butte District production is credited at 24.8B pounds of copper between 1180-20041) and occupies a similar geological setting. Smart Creek is considered prospective for porphyry copper as well as copper-gold-silver enriched carbonate replacement deposits (CRD). 
