GEX Management Publishes Research on Diligence and Revenue Quality in Services Businesses
Press Release
OTC Disclosure & News Service | 09/09/2026
DALLAS, TX — September 09, 2026 — GEX Management, Inc. (OTC: GXXM) this week published three new research pieces in the GEX Knowledge Center, the Company's public library of operating and transaction research. The pieces examine what standard due diligence overlooks in a services business, how recurring revenue gets misclassified, and why a single reported workforce turnover figure can describe two very different companies.
What Diligence Misses in a Services Business. In a services business the risk that matters is rarely on the schedules a buyer asks for. It sits in relationships held by individuals, in work that runs on undocumented habit, in the owner's own unpaid hours, and in how thin the layer below the owner really is. None of those appear in a quality of earnings report, and all of them decide what the business looks like twelve months after closing.
Recurring Revenue That Is Not. Repeat busines"
