otc,otc:f51207b17a01,2026-09-09,IFUS,"","",news,IFUS Letter to Shareholders 9-09-2026,https://www.otcmarkets.com/stock/IFUS/news/IFUS-Letter-to-Shareholders-9-09-2026?id=534391,false,"",7059,"Napoleonville Produc�on Unit 1 (NPU1) Producing Test Bales of SGP+™ - Impact Fusion Interna�onal Retroﬁted Machinery to Boost Produc�on Capacity and Eﬃciency LETTER TO THE SHAREHOLDERS September 9, 2026 Napoleonville, LA IFUS:OTCID The retrofitted Selco/Mosley Badger Double Ram Press has now been officially commissioned with fresh test bales of SGP+™ rolling off the machine. Per design specifications, testing of initial production timing resulted in successful bale production in 18-sec increments, establishing new production capability. Further refinement of the software is underway so as to allow IFUS to achieve optimum bale production in 15-sec increments. With this, a steady-state production cycle of 1-bale / minute has been established as an initial milestone, which in turn will allow IFUS to produce 600-bales in a normal 12-hr shift. This timing allows for IFUS to perform daily routine maintenance on the machine, while also allowing for new processes in bale handling to become “habit-strength”. At present, refinement of the strapping system and bale handling processes are being modified to accommodate this new production capability. This includes the training of operational and maintenance teams to manage this accelerated operational pace. As SGP+™ and SAG™ product demand increases, shorter cycle times for bale production will be established in 5-sec improvement increments until maximum steady-state production cycles are achieved. This requires newly refined processes for handling, storage, and/or immediate Orders-to-Cash loading of the 2200-lb bales being produced. Additionally, the new Nutri-Mastic™ Sprayer System has been lined-out so as to optimize better dispersion into the Sugarcane Bagasse mat. This is resulting in more unform SGP+™ bale production per physical analysis of the bales being produced. With these efforts underway, IFUS has successfully produced bales to initiate: • Quality Assurance and Herd Performance Testing at Deer Run Ranch in Jefferson"
