PolarX Announces Hyper Copper Grades Over Big Widths from Surface Point to Significant Resource Growth at Caribou Dome Project
Follows Recent Announcement of Drilling Hitting Massive Sulphides with Visible Chalocprite Well Outside the Resource at Project
ANCHORAGE, Alaska, Sept. 11, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- PolarX Limited (ASX: PXX; OTCQB: PXXXF) announced exceptional assay results from the first holes for the 2026 diamond drilling campaign at its hyper-grade Caribou Dome Project, part of the Alaska Range Joint Venture with Northern Star Resources Limited in Alaska.
The campaign is fully funded by Northern Star and will be completed by the end of this month with approximately 1,700m of planned drilling remaining.
Assays confirm that holes (CD26-004-CD26-007) intersected exceptionally high-grade copper zones. Both holes also targeted deeper mineralization to the north along the boundary of the hanging wall to test historic drill intercepts.
